# The docs site's local build state (siteDirFor: `docs/`). Until the
# separation these were ignored only by the monorepo root's .gitignore, so a
# standalone clone would `git add -A` a gem tree. Anchored, so the vendored
# assets Jekyll serves (`docs/assets/js/vendor/`, `site-chrome/assets/js/vendor/`)
# stay addable. The Gemfile is the site chrome's (`site-chrome/`), so a bundle
# installed beside it is ignored there too.
